IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`

§ `Chapter 16 -- Kidnapping, abduction, slavery and forced labour`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 359, 360, 361, 362, 364, 365, 366, 367, 368, 370, 371, 372,
-- 373, 373A, 374.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- Shape of the group. s 359 says kidnapping is of two kinds and ss 360 and 361
-- define them; s 362 defines abduction, which is a different thing and not a kind of
-- kidnapping. ss 364 to 367 are each "kidnaps or abducts" plus a purpose, so they
-- share a common opening. s 368 attaches to a kidnapping or abduction committed by
-- someone else. ss 370 to 373A are the slavery and prostitution dealings, which do
-- not require a kidnapping at all, and s 374 stands alone.
--
-- PUNISHMENT IS NOT COMPUTED. ss 363 and 363A are the punishment sections for
-- kidnapping and abduction respectively, and are not encoded; `the person kidnaps`
-- and `the person abducts` are decided here because they are definitions.
-- s 368 punishes "in the same manner as if he had kidnapped or abducted such person
-- with the same intention or knowledge or for the same purpose" -- a punishment
-- direction, so what is decided here is the conduct element only.

§§ `Sections 359, 360 and 361 -- Kidnapping`

-- s 359: kidnapping is of 2 kinds, kidnapping from Singapore and kidnapping from
-- lawful guardianship. It states no test of its own; it is the head under which the
-- two definitions sit, and `the person kidnaps` below is what it amounts to.
--
-- s 360: conveying any person beyond the limits of Singapore without the consent of
-- that person, or of someone legally authorised to consent for them.
-- s 361: taking or enticing a minor below 16, or a person of unsound mind, out of
-- the keeping of the lawful guardian, without that guardian's consent. Its
-- Explanation includes within "lawful guardian" any person lawfully entrusted with
-- the care or custody, which widens what may be asserted and adds no limb.
--
-- The Exception to s 361 is written into the section: it does not extend to a person
-- who in good faith believes himself the father of an illegitimate child, or
-- entitled to its lawful custody, **unless** the act is committed for an immoral or
-- unlawful purpose. That "unless" restores the section, so the Exception is encoded
-- as a good-faith belief that is defeated by an immoral or unlawful purpose.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 360"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes kidnapping from Singapore under Penal Code 1871 section 360
GIVEN k IS A Kidnapping @desc Conveying a person beyond the limits of Singapore without that person's consent or the consent of someone legally authorised to give it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person kidnaps from Singapore` IF
        k's `conveys any person beyond the limits of Singapore`
    AND k's `without the consent of that person or of some person legally authorised to consent on behalf of that person`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 361 Exception"
GIVEN k IS A Kidnapping
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 361 Exception protects the act` IF
        k's `the accused in good faith believes himself to be the father of an illegitimate child or to be entitled to the lawful custody of such child`
    AND (NOT k's `the act is committed for an immoral or unlawful purpose`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 361"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes kidnapping from lawful guardianship under Penal Code 1871 section 361
GIVEN k IS A Kidnapping @desc Taking or enticing a minor below 16, or a person of unsound mind, out of the keeping of the lawful guardian without that guardian's consent, where the section's own good-faith Exception does not protect the act.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person kidnaps from lawful guardianship` IF
        k's `takes or entices any minor below 16 years of age or any person of unsound mind out of the keeping of the lawful guardian of such minor or person`
    AND k's `without the consent of such guardian`
    AND (NOT `the section 361 Exception protects the act` k)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 359"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes kidnapping of either kind under Penal Code 1871 section 359
GIVEN k IS A Kidnapping @desc Kidnapping from Singapore (s 360) or from lawful guardianship (s 361).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person kidnaps` IF
        `the person kidnaps from Singapore` k
    OR  `the person kidnaps from lawful guardianship` k

§§ `Section 362 -- Abduction`

-- Whoever by force compels, or by any deceitful means induces, any person to go from
-- any place. Abduction is not a kind of kidnapping: it needs no minority, no
-- guardian and no crossing of the border, and the person abducted may be an adult
-- who consents to nothing.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 362"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes abduction under Penal Code 1871 section 362
GIVEN k IS A Kidnapping @desc Compelling by force, or inducing by deceitful means, any person to go from any place.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person abducts` IF
    k's `by force compels or by any deceitful means induces any person to go from any place`

§§ `Sections 364 to 367 -- Kidnapping or abducting for a purpose`

-- Each of these four sections opens "Whoever kidnaps or abducts any person", so the
-- disjunction is gathered once. Each then adds its own purpose or knowledge:
-- s 364: in order that the person may be murdered, or so disposed of as to be put in
-- danger of being murdered.
-- s 365: with intent to cause the person to be secretly and wrongfully confined.
-- s 366: a woman, with intent that she be compelled to marry against her will, or
-- knowing it likely that she will be; or in order that she be forced or seduced to
-- illicit intercourse or a life of prostitution, or knowing it likely that she will
-- be so forced or seduced.
-- s 367: in order that the person be subjected, or so disposed of as to be put in
-- danger of being subjected, to grievous hurt or slavery or to non-consensual penile
-- penetration of the anus or mouth, or knowing it likely that he will be.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 359 and 362"
GIVEN k IS A Kidnapping
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person kidnaps or abducts` IF
        `the person kidnaps` k
    OR  `the person abducts` k

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 364"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes kidnapping or abducting in order to murder under Penal Code 1871 section 364
GIVEN k IS A Kidnapping @desc Kidnapping or abduction in order that the person may be murdered or put in danger of being murdered.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes kidnapping or abducting in order to murder` IF
        `the person kidnaps or abducts` k
    AND k's `in order that such person may be murdered or may be so disposed of as to be put in danger of being murdered`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 365"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes kidnapping or abducting with intent secretly and wrongfully to confine under Penal Code 1871 section 365
GIVEN k IS A Kidnapping @desc Kidnapping or abduction with intent to cause the person to be secretly and wrongfully confined.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes kidnapping or abducting to confine secretly` IF
        `the person kidnaps or abducts` k
    AND k's `with intent to cause that person to be secretly and wrongfully confined`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 366"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes kidnapping or abducting a woman to compel marriage or for illicit intercourse under Penal Code 1871 section 366
GIVEN k IS A Kidnapping @desc Kidnapping or abduction of a woman, with intent or knowledge that she will be compelled to marry against her will, or forced or seduced to illicit intercourse or a life of prostitution.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes kidnapping or abducting a woman to compel marriage` IF
        `the person kidnaps or abducts` k
    AND k's `the person kidnapped or abducted is a woman`
    AND (   k's `with intent that she may be compelled or knowing it to be likely that she will be compelled to marry any person against her will`
         OR k's `in order that she may be forced or seduced to illicit intercourse or to a life of prostitution or knowing it to be likely that she will be so forced or seduced`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 367"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes kidnapping or abducting in order to subject a person to grievous hurt or slavery under Penal Code 1871 section 367
GIVEN k IS A Kidnapping @desc Kidnapping or abduction in order that the person be subjected, or put in danger of being subjected, to grievous hurt, slavery or non-consensual penile penetration of the anus or mouth, or knowing it likely.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes kidnapping or abducting to subject to grievous hurt or slavery` IF
        `the person kidnaps or abducts` k
    AND k's `in order that such person may be subjected or so disposed of as to be put in danger of being subjected to grievous hurt or slavery or to non-consensual penile penetration of the anus or mouth or knowing it to be likely that such person will be so subjected or disposed of`

§§ `Section 368 -- Concealing or confining a kidnapped person`

-- Whoever, knowing that any person has been kidnapped or abducted, wrongfully
-- conceals or keeps such person in confinement.
-- s 368 does not require the accused to have done the kidnapping: it attaches to a
-- kidnapping or abduction by someone else, and the knowledge of it is the element.
-- So it does not conjoin `the person kidnaps or abducts`.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 368"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes wrongfully concealing or confining a kidnapped person under Penal Code 1871 section 368
GIVEN k IS A Kidnapping @desc Knowing that a person has been kidnapped or abducted, wrongfully concealing or keeping that person in confinement. The accused need not have committed the kidnapping.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes concealing or confining a kidnapped person` IF
    k's `knowing that any person has been kidnapped or has been abducted wrongfully conceals or keeps such person in confinement`

§§ `Sections 370 and 371 -- Slavery`

-- s 370: importing, exporting, removing, buying, selling or disposing of any person
-- as a slave; or accepting, receiving or detaining against his will any person as a
-- slave. The two limbs differ -- only the second carries "against his will".
-- s 371: habitually importing, exporting, removing, buying, selling, trafficking or
-- dealing in slaves. "Habitually" is the whole of what separates it from s 370.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 370"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes buying or disposing of a person as a slave under Penal Code 1871 section 370
GIVEN k IS A Kidnapping @desc Importing, exporting, removing, buying, selling or disposing of a person as a slave, or accepting, receiving or detaining a person as a slave against his will.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes dealing in a person as a slave` IF
        k's `imports exports removes buys sells or disposes of any person as a slave`
    OR  k's `accepts receives or detains against his will any person as a slave`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 371"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes habitual dealing in slaves under Penal Code 1871 section 371
GIVEN k IS A Kidnapping @desc Habitually importing, exporting, removing, buying, selling, trafficking or dealing in slaves.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes habitual dealing in slaves` IF
    k's `habitually imports exports removes buys sells traffics or deals in slaves`

§§ `Sections 372, 373 and 373A -- Dealing in persons for prostitution`

-- ss 372 and 373 are the sale and the purchase sides of the same transaction, and
-- share everything else: a person below 21, and either an intent that the person be
-- employed or used at any age for prostitution, illicit intercourse or any unlawful
-- and immoral purpose, or knowledge that it is likely.
-- Each section carries a presumption -- that one who disposes of, or obtains
-- possession of, a female below 21 to or from a prostitute or brothel-keeper is
-- presumed until the contrary is proved to have done so for prostitution. Those are
-- rebuttable presumptions of fact, not elements, and are not encoded.
-- s 373A has three limbs of its own, two about bringing a woman into Singapore and
-- one about selling or buying a woman for prostitution. It has no age element.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 372 and 373"
GIVEN k IS A Kidnapping
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prostitution purpose or knowledge is present` IF
        k's `with intent that such person shall at any age be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution or illicit intercourse with any person or for any unlawful and immoral purpose`
    OR  k's `knowing it to be likely that such person will at any age be employed or used for any such purpose`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 372"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes selling a minor for purposes of prostitution under Penal Code 1871 section 372
GIVEN k IS A Kidnapping @desc Selling, letting to hire or otherwise disposing of a person below 21, with the intent or knowledge s 372 requires.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes selling a minor for prostitution` IF
        k's `the person dealt with is below 21 years of age`
    AND k's `sells lets to hire or otherwise disposes of that person`
    AND `the prostitution purpose or knowledge is present` k

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 373"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes buying a minor for purposes of prostitution under Penal Code 1871 section 373
GIVEN k IS A Kidnapping @desc Buying, hiring or otherwise obtaining possession of a person below 21, with the intent or knowledge s 373 requires.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes buying a minor for prostitution` IF
        k's `the person dealt with is below 21 years of age`
    AND k's `buys hires or otherwise obtains possession of that person`
    AND `the prostitution purpose or knowledge is present` k

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 373A"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes importing a woman for purposes of prostitution under Penal Code 1871 section 373A
GIVEN k IS A Kidnapping @desc Bringing a woman into Singapore by false pretence or deceit for prostitution, or to be sold or bought for prostitution, or selling or buying any woman for prostitution.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes importing a woman for prostitution` IF
        k's `by any false pretence false representation or fraudulent or deceitful means brings or assists in bringing into Singapore any woman with intent that she may be employed or used for the purpose of prostitution`
    OR  k's `brings or assists in bringing into Singapore any woman with intent that she may be sold or bought for the purpose of prostitution`
    OR  k's `sells or buys any woman for the purpose of prostitution`

§§ `Section 374 -- Unlawful compulsory labour`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 374"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes unlawful compulsory labour under Penal Code 1871 section 374
GIVEN k IS A Kidnapping @desc Unlawfully compelling a person to labour against that person's will.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes unlawful compulsory labour` IF
    k's `unlawfully compels any person to labour against the will of that person`

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes kidnapping` IF
        `the person kidnaps` (a's `kidnapping`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes abduction` IF
        `the person abducts` (a's `kidnapping`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes dealing in a person as a slave` IF
        (   `constitutes dealing in a person as a slave` (a's `kidnapping`)
         OR `constitutes habitual dealing in slaves` (a's `kidnapping`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes dealing in a person for prostitution` IF
        (   `constitutes selling a minor for prostitution` (a's `kidnapping`)
         OR `constitutes buying a minor for prostitution` (a's `kidnapping`)
         OR `constitutes importing a woman for prostitution` (a's `kidnapping`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes unlawful compulsory labour` IF
        `constitutes unlawful compulsory labour` (a's `kidnapping`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
